      "narrate": {
        "id": "narrate",
        "kind": "composite",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "Read aloud",
        "description": "Express a text content as speech: first the text is rewritten as a narration for reading aloud (text), then, when a speech model is set (argument or setting speech_model, with speech_provider), that narration is spoken (audio). Without a speech model the result is the narration text; no speech adapter is registered by default.",
        "labels": {
          "pl": "Przeczytaj na głos"
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "script",
            "action": "use_model",
            "with": {
              "system": {
                "$localized": {
                  "en": "You prepare texts for reading aloud. Rewrite the text as a spoken narration: short sentences, no markup or lists, numbers and abbreviations written out in words, a clear rhythm. Keep the meaning and the language. Output only the narration.",
                  "pl": "Przygotowujesz teksty do czytania na głos. Przepisz tekst jako narrację mówioną: krótkie zdania, bez znaczników i list, liczby i skróty zapisane słowami, wyraźny rytm. Zachowaj sens i język. Podaj samą narrację."
                }
              },
              "prompt": {
                "$format": {
                  "$localized": {
                    "en": "Prepare the text above for narration. Tone: {tone}.",
                    "pl": "Przygotuj powyższy tekst do narracji. Ton: {tone}."
                  }
                },
                "vars": {
                  "tone": {
                    "$arg": "tone",
                    "default": {
                      "$localized": {
                        "en": "calm and clear",
                        "pl": "spokojny i wyraźny"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "parameters": {
                "temperature": 0.5
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "speak",
            "action": "use_model",
            "when": {
              "arg": "speech_model"
            },
            "with": {
              "model": {
                "$arg": "speech_model"
              },
              "provider": {
                "$arg": "speech_provider",
                "default": ""
              },
              "wants": [
                "audio"
              ],
              "parameters": {
                "$arg": "speech_parameters",
                "default": {}
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "text"
        ],
        "outputs": [
          "text",
          "audio"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "has_text"
        ],
        "produces": [
          "audio_form"
        ],
        "content_op": "preserve",
        "form_op": "express",
        "cost": 1.0,
        "confidence": 0.8,
        "effects": {
          "reads_only": false,
          "writes": true,
          "sends_off_device": true,
          "costs_money": true,
          "irreversible": false,
          "touches_private_data": true
        },
        "consumer": "",
        "phrases": {
          "en": [
            "read aloud",
            "read out",
            "narrate"
          ],
          "pl": [
            "przeczytaj na głos",
            "przeczytaj naglos",
            "opowiedz*",
            "narracj*"
          ]
        },
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "tone",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "default": "calm and clear",
            "description": {
              "en": "Tone of the narration.",
              "pl": "Ton narracji."
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "speech_model",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "setting": "speech_model",
            "description": {
              "en": "A model that speaks (needs an adapter that produces audio). Without it the result is the narration text.",
              "pl": "Model, który mówi (wymaga adaptera dającego dźwięk). Bez niego wynikiem jest tekst narracji."
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "speech_provider",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "setting": "speech_provider",
            "description": {
              "en": "The provider (manifest id) of the speech model.",
              "pl": "Dostawca (id manifestu) modelu mowy."
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "speech_parameters",
            "type": "object",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Extra parameters of the speech request (voice, format ...), as the provider names them.",
              "pl": "Dodatkowe parametry żądania mowy (głos, format ...) w nazwach dostawcy."
            }
          }
        ],
        "examples": {
          "en": [
            "read this message aloud"
          ],
          "pl": [
            "przeczytaj tę wiadomość na głos"
          ]
        }
      },
      "actions.for": {
        "id": "actions.for",
        "kind": "atomic",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "Actions that fit an element",
        "description": "Which actions fit the element: traits it has against the traits each action requires, then the rules of the scope. Each row: status (applicable, needs_confirmation, denied with reason, default) and the explanation.",
        "labels": {
          "pl": "Akcje pasujące do elementu"
        },
        "inputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "outputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "application"
        ],
        "produces": [],
        "content_op": "none",
        "form_op": "none",
        "cost": 0.0,
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "effects": {
          "reads_only": true,
          "writes": false,
          "sends_off_device": false,
          "costs_money": false,
          "irreversible": false,
          "touches_private_data": false
        },
        "consumer": "loom/src/actions/action_rules.cpp",
        "port": "actions",
        "action": "for",
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "element",
            "type": "object",
            "required": true,
            "description": {
              "en": "The element: {\"class\": class id, \"traits\": [extra traits], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": optional}",
              "pl": "Element: {\"class\": id klasy, \"traits\": [dodatkowe cechy], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": opcjonalnie}"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "scope",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Scope level of the scopes chain, or an object {level: instance id}; default: the most specific level",
              "pl": "Poziom łańcucha zakresów albo obiekt {poziom: id}; domyślnie najbardziej szczegółowy"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "include_unmatched",
            "type": "boolean",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Also list actions whose requirements the element does not meet (status not_applicable, with the missing traits)",
              "pl": "Wypisz także akcje, których wymagań element nie spełnia (status not_applicable, z brakującymi cechami)"
            },
            "has_default": true,
            "edit": "toggle",
            "default": false
          }
        ],
        "http": {
          "verb": "POST",
          "path": "/api/actions/for"
        }
      },
      "actions.explain": {
        "id": "actions.explain",
        "kind": "atomic",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "Explain one action for an element",
        "description": "Why an action does or does not fit an element: traits matched or missing (and where each came from), every rule considered and the one that decided; when traits are missing, the chain proposals that would supply them. The thresholds of those proposals come through the scope chain (installation, user, conversation like the rules) and the answer says which scope set each (extrapolation.resolved).",
        "labels": {
          "pl": "Wyjaśnij jedną akcję dla elementu"
        },
        "inputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "outputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "application"
        ],
        "produces": [],
        "content_op": "none",
        "form_op": "none",
        "cost": 0.0,
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "effects": {
          "reads_only": true,
          "writes": false,
          "sends_off_device": false,
          "costs_money": false,
          "irreversible": false,
          "touches_private_data": false
        },
        "consumer": "loom/src/actions/action_rules.cpp",
        "port": "actions",
        "action": "explain",
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "element",
            "type": "object",
            "required": true,
            "description": {
              "en": "The element: {\"class\": class id, \"traits\": [extra traits], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": optional}",
              "pl": "Element: {\"class\": id klasy, \"traits\": [dodatkowe cechy], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": opcjonalnie}"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "action",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": {
              "en": "Action id from the catalogue",
              "pl": "Identyfikator akcji z katalogu"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "choice:actions"
          },
          {
            "name": "scope",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Scope level of the scopes chain, or an object {level: instance id}; default: the most specific level",
              "pl": "Poziom łańcucha zakresów albo obiekt {poziom: id}; domyślnie najbardziej szczegółowy"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          }
        ],
        "http": {
          "verb": "POST",
          "path": "/api/actions/explain"
        }
      },
      "actions.propose_chain": {
        "id": "actions.propose_chain",
        "kind": "atomic",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "Propose a chain of actions",
        "description": "Candidate chains of actions that make a missing trait (or the requirements of a target action) available, ranked by declared cost and confidence and bounded by the extrapolation preset. Proposals only: nothing is executed. The preset and every threshold resolve through the same scope chain as the rules (installation preset, the user's settings extrapolation_preset / extrapolation_bounds, rules with effect set_value on a conversation or a project); the answer carries `resolved` (which scope, rule and initiator set each value) and `scope`.",
        "labels": {
          "pl": "Zaproponuj łańcuch akcji"
        },
        "inputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "outputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "application"
        ],
        "produces": [],
        "content_op": "none",
        "form_op": "none",
        "cost": 0.0,
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "effects": {
          "reads_only": true,
          "writes": false,
          "sends_off_device": false,
          "costs_money": false,
          "irreversible": false,
          "touches_private_data": false
        },
        "consumer": "loom/src/actions/action_rules.cpp",
        "port": "actions",
        "action": "propose_chain",
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "element",
            "type": "object",
            "required": true,
            "description": {
              "en": "The element: {\"class\": class id, \"traits\": [extra traits], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": optional}",
              "pl": "Element: {\"class\": id klasy, \"traits\": [dodatkowe cechy], \"attrs\": {...}, \"id\": opcjonalnie}"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "target_trait",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "The trait the element should get",
              "pl": "Cecha, którą element ma zyskać"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "target_action",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "The action the element should become fit for",
              "pl": "Akcja, do której element ma się nadać"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "choice:actions"
          },
          {
            "name": "scope",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Scope level of the scopes chain, or an object {level: instance id}; default: the most specific level",
              "pl": "Poziom łańcucha zakresów albo obiekt {poziom: id}; domyślnie najbardziej szczegółowy"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "preset",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Extrapolation preset (off disables proposals); absent = the preset the scope chain resolves (installation, user, conversation)",
              "pl": "Preset ekstrapolacji (off wyłącza propozycje); brak = preset, który wyznacza łańcuch zakresów (instalacja, użytkownik, rozmowa)"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "choice:extrapolation_presets"
          },
          {
            "name": "max_length",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Longest chain; absent = the preset value, null = no bound",
              "pl": "Najdłuższy łańcuch; brak = wartość presetu, null = bez ograniczenia"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "max_cost",
            "type": "number",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Largest total declared cost; absent = the preset value, null = no bound",
              "pl": "Największy łączny koszt; brak = wartość presetu, null = bez ograniczenia"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "min_confidence",
            "type": "number",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Lowest total confidence; absent = the preset value, null = no bound",
              "pl": "Najniższa łączna pewność; brak = wartość presetu, null = bez ograniczenia"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "max_results",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "How many chains to return; absent = the preset value, null = all",
              "pl": "Ile łańcuchów zwrócić; brak = wartość presetu, null = wszystkie"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          }
        ],
        "http": {
          "verb": "POST",
          "path": "/api/actions/propose_chain"
        }
      },
      "actions.run": {
        "id": "actions.run",
        "kind": "atomic",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "Run an action",
        "description": "Runs an action (or a chain from actions.propose_chain) on an element: the rules of the scope are asked for every action of the plan, a confirmation pauses the run with a receipt, the usage guard's x10 hold pauses the step with its receipt, every step leaves a record with provenance. propose: true stores the plan and waits for the user's go. Answer: the run document (loom.action_run/1). A completed run stores its result as graph data (a form node of the result's modality, a content node shared per source element, an action_run node) where the setting action_result_target says (graph, run_only, conversation_message; scoped like the rules); long text goes to the blob store. The document tells the nodes in result.produced.",
        "labels": {
          "pl": "Wykonaj akcję"
        },
        "inputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "outputs": [
          "json"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "application"
        ],
        "produces": [],
        "content_op": "none",
        "form_op": "none",
        "cost": 0.0,
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "effects": {
          "reads_only": false,
          "writes": true,
          "sends_off_device": true,
          "costs_money": true,
          "irreversible": false,
          "touches_private_data": true
        },
        "consumer": "loom/src/actions/runner.cpp",
        "port": "actions",
        "action": "run",
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "action",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "The action to run (exactly one of action and chain)",
              "pl": "Akcja do wykonania (dokładnie jedno z: action, chain)"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "choice:actions"
          },
          {
            "name": "chain",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "A chain of steps [{\"action\", \"with\"?}] or a chain object from actions.propose_chain",
              "pl": "Łańcuch kroków [{\"action\", \"with\"?}] albo obiekt łańcucha z actions.propose_chain"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "element",
            "type": "object",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "The element: a bare id (m_..., c_..., a blob hash, a settings key), a class id, or {\"class\", \"traits\", \"attrs\", \"id\"}",
              "pl": "Element: goły identyfikator (m_..., c_..., skrót blobu, klucz ustawienia), id klasy albo {\"class\", \"traits\", \"attrs\", \"id\"}"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "args",
            "type": "object",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Arguments of the action ({\"$arg\": name} in its steps)",
              "pl": "Argumenty akcji ({\"$arg\": nazwa} w jej krokach)"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          },
          {
            "name": "scope",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Scope level of the scopes chain, or an object {level: instance id}; default: the most specific level",
              "pl": "Poziom łańcucha zakresów albo obiekt {poziom: id}; domyślnie najbardziej szczegółowy"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "propose",
            "type": "boolean",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Store the plan and execute nothing until the user says yes",
              "pl": "Zapisz plan i nic nie wykonuj, dopóki użytkownik nie zatwierdzi"
            },
            "has_default": true,
            "edit": "toggle",
            "default": false
          },
          {
            "name": "confirmed",
            "type": "boolean",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "The caller's yes to the confirmations the rules ask for in this plan - honoured only with receipt_id (the plan_receipt of a preview or a proposal of exactly this plan); a bare true returns the proposal instead of running. Denials and the x10 usage confirmation are never covered.",
              "pl": "Tak wywołującego na potwierdzenia, o które proszą reguły w tym planie - uwzględniane tylko z receipt_id (plan_receipt podglądu lub propozycji dokładnie tego planu); samo true zwraca propozycję zamiast wykonać. Odmowy i potwierdzenie ×10 nigdy nie są objęte."
            },
            "has_default": true,
            "edit": "toggle",
            "default": false
          },
          {
            "name": "receipt_id",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "With confirmed: the plan_receipt that actions.preview (or a proposal, propose:true) gave for exactly this plan (action, element, args, scope).",
              "pl": "Razem z confirmed: plan_receipt, który actions.preview (albo propozycja, propose:true) zwróciło dla dokładnie tego planu (akcja, element, argumenty, zakres)."
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "ref",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Who or what confirms (recorded in the run)",
              "pl": "Kto lub co potwierdza (zapisywane w przebiegu)"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "free_text"
          },
          {
            "name": "context",
            "type": "object",
            "required": false,
            "description": {
              "en": "Where the request came from (conv_id, message_id, lang ...); stored with the run. conv_id scopes the rules and the result target to that conversation; lang picks the language of the prompts",
              "pl": "Skąd pochodzi żądanie (conv_id, message_id, lang ...); zapisywane z przebiegiem. conv_id wyznacza zakres reguł i celu wyniku, lang wybiera język promptów"
            },
            "has_default": false,
            "edit": "json"
          }
        ],
        "http": {
          "verb": "POST",
          "path": "/api/actions/run"
        }
      },
